  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "The losing cluster highlights two core structural defects: tight stop-loss whipsaws around the ~0.55% threshold (Trades 1, 2, 3, and 5) where normal intraday mean-reversion noise triggers full-R losses before expansion, and premature breakeven trailing stops (Trades 4 and 6) that exit with negligible gross gains which flip to net losses after ~\u20b94.00 in round-trip transaction fees. Furthermore, late-session entries (Trades 7 and 10) lack sufficient time and directional liquidity to hit the ambitious 1.15% target, resulting in stagnant EOD square-offs eroded by brokerage and STT drag.",
    "learning": "In Indian NSE large-cap cash equities on a \u20b910,000 capital base, fixed brokerage and statutory charges act as a severe tax on breakeven exits and time-decayed afternoon trades; survival requires wider initial stops (0.68%) paired with higher-conviction volume filters (2.45x) and more achievable profit targets (0.95%) to bank clean net gains before midday mean-reversion.",
    "parameter_patch": {
      "min_target_pct": 0.95,
      "min_sweep_vol_multiplier": 2.45,
      "breakeven_trigger_r": 1.05,
      "min_sl_pct": 0.68
    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #24 Post-Mortem & Parameter Mutation\nOut-of-sample testing with DeepSeek V4.1 Flash yielded a 27.3% win rate and a 0.73 Profit Factor, primarily dragged down by \u20b939.38 in transaction fees turning marginal gross wins (Trades #4, #6, #7) into net losses and tight 0.55% stops getting swept by routine 5-minute volatility in high-beta names like `TATASTEEL`. To eliminate low-conviction retail noise and counter fee drag, we are increasing `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` from **2.15x to 2.45x** to demand genuine institutional footprint at entry, and widening `min_sl_pct` from **0.55% to 0.68%** to survive initial liquidity retests. Concurrently, we are relaxing `min_target_pct` from **1.15% to 0.95%** and pushing `breakeven_trigger_r` from **0.85R to 1.05R** so winning trades capture full target extensions rather than choking out at scratch levels where NSE statutory charges guarantee a net loss."
